diff --git a/docs/features/host-vocabulary.md b/docs/features/host-vocabulary.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..213acf6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/features/host-vocabulary.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# Pinned Host vocabulary tables (candidate)
+
+`--embedding-residency host` keeps the stored token table in pinned system RAM.
+`--output-head-residency host` does the same for the full target output head.
+Each defaults to `device`. The optimized speculative proposal head stays on the GPU.
+The Qwen3.5-family loader uses the existing artifact Pinned materialization and its
+owned `PinnedHostBuffer`; CUDA kernels read those stable addresses through unified
+addressing. Arithmetic still runs on NVIDIA. No CPU linear-product path, weight
+transcode, file rewrite, or hidden device copy is introduced by these options.
+
+The candidate supports stored Q8_G32_FP16 vocabulary matrices; other formats and
+vocabulary-transcode flags are rejected. These options require CUDA unified
+addressing and exclude Vision overlay. Resident
+and CPU Vision remain available. Other model families reject the options explicitly.
+The pinned allocation remains owned by the model, including during suspend/resume.
+Device and pinned-host bytes must be reported separately.
+
+GPU access to RAM uses the host link, so freeing VRAM can cost throughput. In
+particular, reading the full output head can be expensive. This is a capacity
+candidate, not an established speed improvement or an automatically applied profile.
+Native context, KV precision, actual residency and memory-floor checks still apply.
+
+`ninfer_host_vocabulary_test` exercises the actual Q8 248320-by-5120 table through
+GPU embedding graph replay and output-head projection at widths 1, 8 and 17. It
+checks pinned pointer attributes and independent represented-code/FP64 oracles.
+Whole-model forward, long-context quality and measured throughput are separate gates.
diff --git a/docs/features/nvfp4-dflash2.md b/docs/features/nvfp4-dflash2.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ac14a52
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/features/nvfp4-dflash2.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Weight-only NVFP4 DFlash2 runtime
+
+This standalone runtime branch supports the 34 NVFP4 objects in the Qwen3.8-27B DFlash2 module.
+It adds execution/binding support for attention projections, context materialization,
+dynamic convolution, linear/SwiGLU projections and the candidate-selector path.
+Module execution uses weight-only NVFP4 with BF16 activations, not invented A4 calibration.
+It preserves tile-aligned NVFP4 subview scale offsets and admits lookup codebooks
+without requiring activation Use metadata that conversion does not produce.
+
+Use a compatible `.ninfer` artifact with a DFlash2 component and select
+`--spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 7`; see [DFlash semantics](../maintainer/dflash.md).
+This patch contains neither a converter recipe nor Windows, HQ or long-context changes.
+Conversion allocation and model-quality qualification remain separate from runtime support.
diff --git a/docs/features/packed56-kv.md b/docs/features/packed56-kv.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..29d322b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/features/packed56-kv.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Packed Q5_1 and Q6_0 KV (candidate implementation)
+
+`--kv-dtype q5_1` selects affine five-bit keys and values. `q6_0` selects symmetric
+six-bit keys and values. These are KV formats, independent of model-weight formats.
+Both currently serve the Qwen D256 attention geometries H16/KV2 and H24/KV4.
+Other model families require their own qualification; this does not enable Gemma KV.
+
+A vector is split into eight consecutive groups of 32 BF16 inputs. Each group is
+stored as a little-endian bitstream of 20 or 24 bytes. Codes never cross groups.
+Scales are separate FP16 planes, indexed by group within each page/token/head.
+This is NInfer's own plane layout, not a byte-compatible GGML block import.
+
+Q5_1: `m = FP16_RNE(min(x))`, `s = FP16_RNE((max(x)-FP32(m))/31)`;
+`q = clamp(RNE_even((x-FP32(m))/FP32(s)),0,31)` (zero when s=0).
+The scale plane stores `(s,m)` for every group; represented values are `q*s+m`.
+Q6_0: `s = FP16_RNE(max(abs(x))/31)`;
+`q = clamp(RNE_even(x/FP32(s)),-31,31)` (zero when s=0), stored as six-bit two's
+complement. The -32 code is not emitted. Represented values are `q*s`.
+The supported finite BF16 inputs must yield finite FP16 scales/offsets.
+Attention rounds decoded operands to BF16 before multiplication, then accumulates
+scores and split softmax in FP32. Wide prefill reuses the BF16 tiled MMA path.
+No cache-wide BF16 expansion or additional persistent allocation is performed.
+
+Per D256 K or V vector: Q5_1 has 160 code bytes + 32 scale/offset bytes (6 bits/value
+including metadata); Q6_0 has 192 code bytes + 16 scale bytes (6.5 bits/value).
+Page padding and allocator alignment are additional and must appear in memory reports.
+Existing context-store byte-plane transfer/checkpoint paths use these actual layouts.
+DFlash2's private cyclic drafter cache remains BF16; these options select target KV.
+
+Tests: `ninfer_packed56_test` checks an independent scalar encoder and bit decoder,
+FP64 attention, permuted pages, the 63/64 boundary, ragged query tiles, masking and
+both decode and tiled-prefill routes. Production artifact and long-context
+qualification are separate requirements. This implementation is unqualified until
+those tests and real-artifact admission pass; no speed claim is established.
